# Cloudflare Pages cache headers (served from /_headers).
#
# Why the catch-all: the SSG build emits 49 HTML files at clean URLs — /about,
# /projects/<slug>, /marketplace/<slug>/demo — not just "/" and "/index.html".
# Rules naming only those two leave the other 47 on Cloudflare's default
# caching, so a returning visitor gets the previous deploy's HTML. That HTML
# points at an /assets/<hash> chunk which no longer exists on the current
# deployment, the chunk 404s, hydration never runs, and the client-side page
# loader never dismisses. Stale HTML and the black screen are the same bug.
#
# Matching rules STACK, and a header set by two rules is joined with a comma.
# So every rule below first strips the inherited value with "! Cache-Control"
# and only then sets its own — without that, /assets/* would inherit no-cache
# and lose its immutable caching entirely.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Vite content-hashes these filenames, so a given URL never changes contents.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/image/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/mascots/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/demos/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/api/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-store
